WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.670
In a world where workplace
diversity sessions

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.700
increasingly resemble
Maoist struggle sessions,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.370
Chloé Valdary's theory
of enchantment seminars

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.400
seek to bring people together
using popular culture,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.490
to explore our common humanity

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.330
and to generate empathy
rather than division.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.560
The 28 year old Valdary started a group

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.010
to combat antisemitism as an undergrad

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.040
at the University of New Orleans,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.300
and after a fellowship at

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.560
the Wall Street Journal's opinion page,

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.550
she created Theory of
Enchantment as an alternative

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.900
to the anti-racist programs of people

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.280
like Ibram X. Kendi and Robin DiAngelo.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.400
Valdary thinks that these programs often

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.480
deepen the very resentments
they seek to alleviate.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.450
Her program on the other
hand employs materials

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.840
as varied as Disney's Lion
King, music by Kendrick Lamar,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.810
and writing from James
Baldwin and Cheryl Strayed.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.600
She spoke to reason about
how her life experiences

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.440
informed Theory of Enchantment,

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.230
why the demand for her program is growing,

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.700
and why she's optimistic about the future

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.610
of race relations and individualism.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.580
Here is Chloé Valdary.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.550
Chloé Valdary, thanks
for talking to Reason.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.880
Thank you for inviting
me, Nick, I appreciate it.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.200
So let's start with the
theory of enchantment.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.500
Give me the capsule summary.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.520
What's the elevator pitch
of a theory of enchantment?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.040
So theory of enchantment is a startup.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.700
It's my company, and we teach anti-racism

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.670
in the corporate boardroom and beyond,

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.130
and we have a very specific approach

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:34.130
to this particular practice
that combines popular culture,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:39.330
the arts, with a kind of
mindfulness, understanding

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.160
of how to fight again and
combat prejudice and bigotry.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.660
What's the landscape,

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.030
say in like corporations and offices?

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.890
I mean, is racism

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:50.723
afoot?

00:01:50.723 --> 00:01:53.070
I mean, is it like a wildfire?

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.750
Is it a muted, you know, smoldering?

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.560
Is it, you know,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.213
how bad is the problem that
you're kind of talking about?

00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:05.240
Yeah, this is actually a
challenging question for me,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.230
because

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.660
on one level,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:12.560
it's not as if companies
are being bombarded with,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.460
you know, the spirit of Jim Crow, right.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.343
That's not what we're talking about here,

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.350
and to that point, as I'm sure you know,

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.230
there's been a giant proliferation of

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.790
diversity and inclusion programs

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.300
over the past year and a half due to

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.060
some of the events of last year.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.810
So you would think, or one would assume,

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.927
that because of that proliferation,

00:02:35.927 --> 00:02:40.780
there's actually not much
prejudice in the workplace.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.380
There's not much bias in the workplace,

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.010
but the problem is that
because a lot of the trainings

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.020
that exist, because a lot of the trainings

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.250
that are super popular
today are in some ways

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.690
creating

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.100
results that end up

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.200
promoting prejudice,

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.110
you have this by-product effect where

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.610
people are actually being
inundated with a kind of approach

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:08.180
to anti-racism that creates

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.300
the likelihood of more
prejudice, not less.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:15.090
So that's like people like
Ibram Kendi or Robin DiAngelo

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.990
are probably the two best
known kind of mascots

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:21.880
for this approach where, you know,
everything, every situation is actually
fraught with a massive amount of

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.260
unacknowledged racism and the job of

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.810
the kind of facilitators
to come in, you know,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.720
and in Robin DiAngelo's
new book Nice Racism

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.220
it's like to come into, you
know, like NPR headquarters.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.330
I'd love to see her come in
and, you know, and just be like,

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.540
you know, you guys are the worst

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.300
because you don't
acknowledge you're racist,

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.040
but you're saying that's
part of the problem

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.340
that your program is trying to

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.030
kind of work around or get past.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.720
Yes, because it's based
upon a couple of things

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.650
that are problematic,

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.570
a couple of ideas that are problematic.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:02.030
If you believe that
anything and everything

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:05.270
is white supremacy, for
example, as it seems to me,

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.550
especially individuals like
Robin DiAngelo believe,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.150
then you are sort of
ironically actually claiming

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.270
that white supremacy is this all powerful,

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.340
all pervasive thing.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.180
You're actually accepting a premise

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:21.070
that white supremacists profess,

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.950
and in doing so you sort
of perpetuate this belief

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:28.780
or this stereotype that people of color

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.450
are helpless victims and will
always be helpless victims,

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.510
and that creates a caricaturing

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.190
of both black and white people,

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.070
which actually just leads to
more prejudice in the workplace

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.650
as opposed to getting rid of it,

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:44.530
and then, you know, the second
thing I'd say that that does

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.530
is that that has a cultural
effect in the long run,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.910
because people are
essentially asking themselves,

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.790
or saying to themselves, I
want to be a good person,

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.750
I want to do the right thing,
this is super in vogue,

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.470
and this is what I'm being
told makes me a good person,

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.340
so it just metastasizes

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:03.780
and it has more giant effect
than it would otherwise,

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.230
perhaps in a, you know,
in a non-digital age.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:10.640
So let's say, you know,
I run a corporation

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:14.110
and, you know, I want to
bring in you in order to

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.340
kind of facilitate

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:21.090
better relationships across
my corporation or whatever.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.040
How do you proceed?

